CHANGES made to the CRYPTOGAMS output (2026-10-26), all by the recipe:
  - only the AVX2 block functions, SHA-256's SHA-extension function and
    the constant tables are kept. The run-time dispatcher (which reads
    OpenSSL's `OPENSSL_ia32cap_P`), the SSSE3, AVX and XOP paths and SHA-512's
    SHA512-extension path are dropped;
  - the functions are renamed `zl_sha2_sha256_avx2`, `zl_sha2_sha256_shaext`
    and `zl_sha2_sha512_avx2` and made `.weak` + `.hidden`, and every local
    label gets the prefix
    `.Lzl_sha256_` / `.Lzl_sha512_`, as do the tables;
  - the `.note.gnu.property` section is dropped, and a `.align 64` is
    restated before each table (upstream it precedes the table's `.type`
    line);
  - a four-line provenance header is added to each file.
The instructions themselves are unchanged.

